WEBVTT

00:00.521 --> 00:03.106
JULY 15TH (THURS) 10:43 AM

00:04.191 --> 00:06.443
Now who is this? I've never
seen this man in my life.

00:06.527 --> 00:07.986
Good afternoon.

00:08.070 --> 00:11.740
I'm Kinoto, the architect.
I believe you called me earlier.

00:12.074 --> 00:13.909
I'm here to give an assessment of

00:13.951 --> 00:15.494
the fire restoration
and renovation.

00:15.577 --> 00:19.163
That's right. We did agree to meet.

00:20.791 --> 00:21.917
Heaven's Door!

00:24.920 --> 00:26.504
My apologies for
the forceful greeting,

00:26.588 --> 00:28.965
but I've reason to be cautious.

00:29.466 --> 00:33.966
YES! THIS GIG'S IN THE BAG!
TIME TO MAKE SOME MONEY!
ROHAN KISHIBE MUST BE LOADED.
I'M GONNA MAKE A KILLING.
I'll JUST CHARGE A LITTLE BIT MORE
AND HOPE HE BITES.

00:29.967 --> 00:33.261
Born in 1970, top notch architect.

00:33.303 --> 00:34.804
Name, Masazo Kinoto.

00:34.847 --> 00:35.827
I see.

00:36.181 --> 00:38.516
He's definitely the man I called.

00:38.600 --> 00:40.810
Nothing points to him being
a Stand user or enemy.

00:41.353 --> 00:42.479
<i>Hm?</i>

00:42.354 --> 00:43.563
I HATE IT WHEN PEOPLE
LOOK AT MY BACK.

00:43.605 --> 00:48.105
I REALLY DON'T WANT ANYONE
PEEKING AT MY BACK.
IT'S NOT LIKE I HAVE ZITS OR
WEIRD SCARS OR A TATTOO,
I JUST DON'T WANT ANYBODY
LOOKING AT MY BACK!
I CAN'T GET A GIRLFRIEND.
WHAT AM I GONNA DO?!

00:49.111 --> 00:50.758
None of this makes any sense,

00:50.821 --> 00:51.571
then again,

00:51.613 --> 00:54.032
no one's without their own
bizarre fears and phobias.

00:54.491 --> 00:58.244
Well, he seems safe enough
to let in the house.

00:58.453 --> 01:01.038
That Rosham-boy seemed
pretty innocent, too…

01:01.123 --> 01:05.127
In any case, a simple,
I can't attack Rohan, can't hurt.

01:06.628 --> 01:10.006
Huh? I didn't just make
a major faux pas did I?

01:10.174 --> 01:14.011
No. Please, come in. Let's talk.

01:17.347 --> 01:18.473
Something wrong?

01:18.599 --> 01:20.934
You'll find most of the fire damage
in the room facing the yard.

01:21.226 --> 01:23.811
You can't perform an assessment
standing out there.

01:23.937 --> 01:27.190
Oh, no, you should go ahead.
I'll follow behind.

01:27.441 --> 01:28.442
Huh?

01:35.657 --> 01:38.201
Now, please, go ahead.

01:42.039 --> 01:44.416
JULY 15TH (THURS) 9:06 AM

01:45.042 --> 01:49.379
EPISODE 32
JULY 15TH (THURS), PART 2

01:45.083 --> 01:47.919
You know,
my escape couldn't be easier.

01:48.003 --> 01:49.400
You fools still haven't figured out
where Yoshikage Kira went, have you?

01:54.343 --> 01:57.012
You don't even know
what I look like.

01:57.054 --> 01:59.139
You never thought my name
was just a little fishy?

01:59.181 --> 02:01.266
You do know
it's Toyohiro Kanedaichi.

02:01.350 --> 02:03.101
W-What the hell?

02:03.185 --> 02:05.562
You're wearing some kind of mask?

02:06.104 --> 02:08.064
I didn't only think about
leaving this thing…

02:08.106 --> 02:10.900
I planned for a clean escape.

02:11.109 --> 02:14.070
Well, I suppose I should
bid you sayonara.

02:14.196 --> 02:15.822
Y-You piece of—

02:16.031 --> 02:18.074
Please stay outside, Mr. Josuke.

02:19.201 --> 02:20.994
I will remain here,
within this tower.

02:21.161 --> 02:23.496
What?!
What the hell's gotten into you?

02:23.747 --> 02:26.833
We're in this situation
because I discovered the tower.

02:26.959 --> 02:30.087
I'm like this now because I decided
to transform into the power line

02:30.170 --> 02:32.255
and climb to this position here.

02:32.589 --> 02:34.674
I wanted you to think I was useful.

02:34.883 --> 02:38.678
I wanted to change your opinion,
for you to be proud of me.

02:38.720 --> 02:41.180
Okuyasu did say to butt out.

02:41.640 --> 02:43.391
I brought this upon myself.

02:45.102 --> 02:46.603
Don't trouble yourselves
on my behalf.

02:46.728 --> 02:49.230
If I imagine this as the interior
of a spaceship,

02:49.273 --> 02:50.899
it actually feels quite roomy.

02:52.192 --> 02:55.153
You're a weirdo,
and a brave one at that.

02:55.320 --> 02:59.532
Though I really don't care
who stays here.

02:59.574 --> 03:01.826
As long as I'm outta here,
I'm happy.

03:01.910 --> 03:03.786
The rest is up to you fool—

03:03.870 --> 03:06.706
Nope, you're the only one
setting up camp in this dump.

03:07.332 --> 03:11.044
The only one delivering
the final "sayonara"

03:11.753 --> 03:15.339
will be from us to you, buddy!

03:15.424 --> 03:16.883
J-Josuke!

03:16.925 --> 03:18.551
Y-You mother—

03:22.514 --> 03:24.307
Thanks to you cutting this line,

03:24.391 --> 03:26.434
I was able to fix it
and get myself up here.

03:26.935 --> 03:28.061
You're amaz—

03:28.103 --> 03:31.523
Mikitaka, give me about
ten seconds, okay?

03:31.606 --> 03:33.608
After I hang this d-bag out to dry

03:33.650 --> 03:35.234
and put him back in his cage
where he belongs,

03:35.277 --> 03:36.945
I'll heal you
like nothing happened.

03:37.112 --> 03:39.781
Don't fall, Josuke!

03:39.948 --> 03:41.407
Of course I won't fall.

03:42.117 --> 03:46.412
I may've said you're amazing,
but I misspoke.

03:46.455 --> 03:49.374
What I should have said
is you're a total moron.

03:49.624 --> 03:52.835
I was content simply
leaving this place.

03:52.878 --> 03:56.381
It never crossed my mind
to kill any one of you…

03:56.965 --> 04:00.468
But now I'm gonna have to
push you to your death

04:00.510 --> 04:03.679
before I can make my getaway,
you idiot!

04:03.764 --> 04:04.890
Shut the hell up!

04:24.368 --> 04:26.119
Shining Diamond…

04:26.161 --> 04:29.747
Up close,
it's pretty damn impressive.

04:29.873 --> 04:31.708
You really think
you stand a chance against me…

04:31.792 --> 04:36.292
I can prance around the top of
this tower with my eyes closed.

04:37.005 --> 04:39.716
I'm guessing its range
is about two meters.

04:50.060 --> 04:51.394
What the hell!

04:51.603 --> 04:54.314
Hey, dumb-ass!
You better cut that out!

04:57.692 --> 04:59.568
Mr. Josuke,
I advise you to move, quickly!

04:59.653 --> 05:01.780
He already slashed it
with his knife!

05:01.863 --> 05:04.073
He already carved slits
into the beam!

05:09.913 --> 05:11.915
That was a real low blow,
you know that!

05:11.998 --> 05:16.498
But you're still not fast enough to
make my Shining Diamond sweat.

05:19.214 --> 05:21.132
What are you smirking at,
you jungle gym freak?

05:21.216 --> 05:24.260
Can't wait for the ass-whooping
I'm about to give you?!

05:24.344 --> 05:26.596
I know every centimeter
of this tower

05:26.638 --> 05:28.514
like the back of my hand.

05:28.598 --> 05:30.725
I know exactly which angle to cut

05:30.767 --> 05:34.145
to send the projectile
in exactly the direction I desire.

05:35.105 --> 05:37.524
Like a pool shark who's bored
with his own mastery,

05:37.566 --> 05:40.151
I know all the moves!

05:40.235 --> 05:41.527
<i>Pool shark?</i>

05:42.737 --> 05:43.404
Jo…

05:43.405 --> 05:44.697
Josuke!

05:47.242 --> 05:51.579
Not fast enough to make
Shining Diamond sweat, huh?

05:51.621 --> 05:54.874
But do you know where
the projectiles are coming from?

05:55.250 --> 05:57.961
Now how many more shots
did I fire off back there…

05:58.044 --> 06:00.463
They're ricochetting off the beams
as I speak.

06:01.506 --> 06:03.257
Here they come!

06:05.594 --> 06:06.428
Mr. Josuke!

06:06.470 --> 06:08.263
Behind you!

06:13.268 --> 06:14.310
Mr. Josuke!

06:15.812 --> 06:18.564
That's why I called you
a total moron.

06:18.607 --> 06:20.650
That alien guy over there

06:20.734 --> 06:23.153
at least had the balls
to say he'd stay behind.

06:23.236 --> 06:25.279
You should have
just listened to him.

06:25.322 --> 06:27.407
You could have lived.

06:29.326 --> 06:30.994
B-Both of his arms?

06:31.036 --> 06:33.621
There's no way he'll
be able to dodge another onslaught.

06:33.663 --> 06:36.332
Now for the famous finishing blow!

06:36.458 --> 06:39.169
- I think I'll aim for your…
- By the way, Okuyasu,

06:39.252 --> 06:41.504
this guy's projectile thingies…

06:41.630 --> 06:44.841
Did ya catch how many of them
I knocked back

06:44.925 --> 06:46.176
with Shining Diamond?

06:46.218 --> 06:48.511
Huh? Yeah, I saw.

06:48.553 --> 06:51.931
You definitely got four of them.

06:52.307 --> 06:54.475
What? What was that nonchalant
"by the way"?

06:54.518 --> 06:57.979
Four of them, huh?
Well, that should be plenty.

06:58.146 --> 07:00.189
Four shots should be
more than enough.

07:00.273 --> 07:02.275
What are you idiots
blathering about?!

07:02.484 --> 07:05.361
You mentioned the word ricochet.

07:05.529 --> 07:07.906
That you ricocheted
your Stand's energy

07:07.989 --> 07:09.448
like a bunch of billiard balls.

07:09.783 --> 07:11.701
That's what you said.

07:11.785 --> 07:14.537
Yeah, I did, what are you
gonna do about it, Josuke?!

07:14.621 --> 07:17.373
My Stand's called Shining Diamond.

07:17.457 --> 07:19.542
I'm guessing that old guy
in the photo told you,

07:19.626 --> 07:22.962
it can correct destroyed matter
and fractured energy.

07:23.171 --> 07:25.214
Correct…
Did I hear you say "correct"?

07:25.298 --> 07:27.341
What the hell did you correct?!

07:27.676 --> 07:30.053
Are you saying you had
the spare time

07:30.136 --> 07:31.387
to correct something just now?

07:31.471 --> 07:33.473
Come on, you're a fool!

07:35.392 --> 07:37.977
He corrected the energy
ricocheting between the beams,

07:38.019 --> 07:41.147
reversing its path so that it
returned to the slashed steel.

07:41.231 --> 07:43.733
Mr. Josuke,
I thought you were done for,

07:44.025 --> 07:45.735
but you had already won.

07:45.819 --> 07:47.779
You're amazing…

07:47.862 --> 07:50.197
I guess you didn't
misspoke after all,

07:50.240 --> 07:51.783
you really do think I'm "amazing."

08:00.000 --> 08:01.710
Please forgive me.

08:01.751 --> 08:03.961
I only started living here
in this tower

08:04.045 --> 08:06.255
to get away from other people.

08:06.381 --> 08:08.383
But the older man in the photograph

08:08.466 --> 08:11.177
said that as long as I could
trap a Stand user,

08:11.219 --> 08:15.056
he'd make sure I could
have a life in the outside world,

08:15.098 --> 08:16.766
so I decided to go for it…

08:16.850 --> 08:18.935
Please! Will you be
so gracious as to let me

08:19.019 --> 08:21.146
go back inside
the safety of the tower?

08:21.229 --> 08:24.357
I never want to
have to leave again.

08:25.358 --> 08:27.943
I just want to live out my life
between these beams.

08:28.028 --> 08:30.989
I'll never contemplate
leaving this place ever again.

08:31.156 --> 08:35.656
MORIOH LANDMARK NO. 9:
THE MAN IN THE ELECTRICAL TOWER

08:31.406 --> 08:35.284
<i>New Morioh landmark:
the man in the electrical tower.</i>

08:35.660 --> 08:38.120
<i>He is a marvel of self-sufficiency,</i>

08:38.204 --> 08:39.830
<i>but bring him
a bit of salt or snacks,</i>

08:39.914 --> 08:41.874
<i>he'll be more than happy
to let you take a picture.</i>

08:42.250 --> 08:44.752
<i>But be warned, he is timid.</i>

08:44.794 --> 08:46.504
<i>He wears a mask and
will not divulge his real name.</i>

08:47.213 --> 08:48.297
I appreciate the confession,

08:48.340 --> 08:49.841
but about the old guy
in the photograph…

08:49.924 --> 08:51.800
Did he say anything else?

08:51.926 --> 08:55.471
Like the whereabouts of his son,
Yoshikage Kira, or anything else?

08:57.766 --> 09:02.266
Is there a Stand user named
Koichi here in Morioh?

09:03.146 --> 09:05.106
What do you know about Koichi?!

09:05.148 --> 09:06.566
Hey, take it easy,

09:06.608 --> 09:09.277
the old guy and I were only
having a casual conversation,

09:09.319 --> 09:11.321
he barely mentioned him.

09:11.404 --> 09:15.904
I didn't think to ask anything,
and he didn't elaborate.

09:16.034 --> 09:18.828
Well, what did he say
about Koichi?!

09:19.329 --> 09:21.998
That he has eliminated him.

09:23.375 --> 09:24.876
What?!

09:25.293 --> 09:27.169
It seems the old guy
in the photograph

09:27.253 --> 09:30.381
had already found his son,
Yoshikage Kira.

09:30.507 --> 09:33.218
He said, from now on, he would
do more than just protect his son,

09:33.301 --> 09:35.845
he said he would start
seeking out and attacking others.

09:35.929 --> 09:38.056
Then he said a new Stand user

09:38.139 --> 09:40.808
eliminated a Stand user
named Koichi just this morning…

09:40.850 --> 09:42.893
That's all he said.

09:44.688 --> 09:48.191
JULY 15TH (THURS) 10:58 AM

09:46.481 --> 09:48.212
Hmm… This will be…

09:49.317 --> 09:53.779
My goodness! Look at this door…
this will be about 800,000 yen!

09:53.822 --> 09:55.448
And look at that,
it's designed in the vein of

09:55.490 --> 09:56.991
either the Victorian
or Edwardian era!

09:57.033 --> 10:00.036
It even uses
English-made materials…

10:00.328 --> 10:02.371
This is going to be quite…

10:02.622 --> 10:05.207
<i>So he doesn't want anyone
looking a this back…</i>

10:05.500 --> 10:07.710
<i>Maybe that explains
his odd behavior</i>

10:07.794 --> 10:10.046
<i>when he first visited my home?</i>

10:11.840 --> 10:12.715
Here you go.

10:12.757 --> 10:14.216
Oh, thank you.

10:14.342 --> 10:15.551
Before it gets cold.

10:15.635 --> 10:17.762
Oh, I'll be fine.

10:20.390 --> 10:22.934
JULY 15TH (THURS) 11:16 AM

10:37.073 --> 10:38.616
<i>I must resist…</i>

10:39.117 --> 10:40.952
<i>Now is not the time…</i>

10:46.791 --> 10:49.502
SHINING DIAMOND

10:49.544 --> 10:52.046
JULY 15TH (THURS) 10:20 AM

10:57.719 --> 11:02.219
I really hope they find
Koichi safe and sound…

11:05.560 --> 11:08.771
JULY 15TH (THURS) 11:37 AM

11:11.483 --> 11:15.445
Damn it! Where is he!
He's not at home, at school,

11:15.528 --> 11:17.154
or any damn place!

11:17.238 --> 11:20.449
Koichi! Koichi!

11:20.533 --> 11:22.785
Where are you, Koichi?!

11:22.911 --> 11:24.787
I'm not giving up!

11:24.829 --> 11:29.329
I'll do whatever it takes, Koichi!

11:29.918 --> 11:31.920
So that's the story.

11:32.045 --> 11:34.589
With your scent-tracking ability,

11:34.631 --> 11:37.467
I wanna know
if you'll help me find Koichi,

11:37.550 --> 11:38.759
Yuya Fungami.

11:40.094 --> 11:44.181
I'll get rid of your injuries,
that's the deal.

11:44.349 --> 11:46.476
That's the deal?

11:46.518 --> 11:48.770
I'm warning you,
don't mess with me, Josuke!

11:48.812 --> 11:50.897
I don't play around!

11:50.939 --> 11:54.317
I'll never forgive you
for doing this to me!

11:54.400 --> 11:56.318
You think I, Yuya Fungami,

11:56.361 --> 11:59.405
would sacrifice my pride
to help you?

11:59.447 --> 12:00.990
So it is a no.

12:01.032 --> 12:03.534
I knew it was a total long shot.

12:03.785 --> 12:05.953
Well, see ya.
I'm kinda short on time.

12:06.079 --> 12:09.165
Wait, huh?! So you're gonna
leave just like that?

12:09.415 --> 12:10.999
W-Wait a second, hey!

12:11.042 --> 12:13.335
Come on, you're not gonna
even give me a chance to bargain…

12:13.628 --> 12:17.632
Okay, fine! I'll help you out!

12:17.674 --> 12:20.510
Jeez, guess I don't really
have a choice…

12:20.593 --> 12:22.011
Shit, I could hold out,

12:22.053 --> 12:25.014
but then I'd just be stuck
in this dump even longer.

12:25.265 --> 12:26.432
I can't give my girls

12:26.474 --> 12:28.642
the kind of attention they deserve
while I'm like this,

12:28.685 --> 12:31.020
for all I know they could be
on their way out,

12:31.104 --> 12:33.564
I'm lonely and worried sick.

12:33.857 --> 12:36.025
Besides, the accident
that got me into this whole mess

12:36.067 --> 12:37.693
is my own doing,

12:37.777 --> 12:39.445
I've got nothing against you.

12:39.821 --> 12:42.615
Now can you hurry up and heal me?

12:42.657 --> 12:44.492
These injuries are
driving me crazy!

12:44.534 --> 12:48.329
Shining Diamond already
reversed your injuries.

12:48.496 --> 12:49.538
Huh?

12:56.796 --> 12:58.380
There's that face…

12:58.882 --> 13:02.135
I am stunningly beautiful,
aren't I…

13:02.260 --> 13:06.305
Beautiful as a Michelangelo
sculpture, at the very least.

13:06.431 --> 13:10.518
But my eyes look
slightly droopy now…

13:10.852 --> 13:13.646
Does your Stand
actually fix things 100%?

13:13.688 --> 13:15.231
Count your blessings, prick!

13:15.398 --> 13:19.235
Now, just how well does
your sense of smell work?

13:19.485 --> 13:20.819
Let's see… I mean,

13:20.862 --> 13:24.490
I can't promise you I'm as good
as some hunting dog or anything…

13:24.699 --> 13:25.449
SNIFF
SNIFF
SNIFF

13:27.076 --> 13:28.535
For example,

13:28.578 --> 13:31.747
I can tell that three girls are
walking up the hall right now.

13:31.831 --> 13:34.667
It smells like
Reiko, Akemi, and Yoshie.

13:34.709 --> 13:36.210
They're my fan girls.

13:37.337 --> 13:40.715
I can tell they're coming back
from the pachinko place.

13:43.259 --> 13:45.052
Hey, Yu-babe! So?

13:46.054 --> 13:49.932
Ah, Yu! Yu is out of bed!

13:49.974 --> 13:50.933
Yo.

13:51.017 --> 13:52.727
Yu baby, you're back…

13:52.769 --> 13:53.978
Yu sweetie!

13:54.062 --> 13:57.190
There, there,
my sweet little vixens.

13:58.775 --> 13:59.901
So you're Josuke!

13:59.943 --> 14:01.361
Why the hell're you here?

14:01.402 --> 14:03.404
Want me to skewer you right here?

14:03.446 --> 14:06.323
Enough. I hold no ill will
toward Josuke now.

14:06.699 --> 14:07.783
Onto more important matters,

14:07.825 --> 14:09.993
you gals just got back
from pachinko, correct?

14:10.119 --> 14:10.828
Huh?

14:10.828 --> 14:12.663
How did you know?

14:12.789 --> 14:15.625
Cause, the part where your skirts
and asses touch reek of sweat.

14:15.708 --> 14:18.043
Where else would you be
planting your cheeks down

14:18.086 --> 14:19.962
on vinyl chairs for so long…

14:20.254 --> 14:22.798
Akemi, got any chocolate?

14:22.840 --> 14:24.299
You won at pachinko, right?

14:24.384 --> 14:27.303
You're right! You're amazing, Yu.

14:27.345 --> 14:29.180
Here, a little souvenir.

14:29.347 --> 14:33.847
As you can see,
I am who I am thanks to them.

14:34.936 --> 14:37.772
You helped me get back on my feet,
you have my support.

14:37.814 --> 14:40.107
Not as good as some hunting dog?

14:40.316 --> 14:42.944
You're a helluva lot better,
Yuya Fungami!

14:42.819 --> 14:46.072
JULY 15TH (THURS) 12:05 PM

14:45.405 --> 14:46.093
Is there something wrong, Sir?

14:47.031 --> 14:49.324
The upstairs floor sustained
fire damage as well, right?

14:49.492 --> 14:52.995
I'll perform the estimate,
so please go ahead.

14:53.037 --> 14:54.830
<i>What is this man doing?</i>

14:54.956 --> 14:57.750
<i>What could be driving him to be
so obsessive about hiding his back?</i>

14:58.001 --> 14:59.711
<i>If I see it, then what?</i>

15:04.799 --> 15:06.383
<i>I have to see it!</i>

15:06.467 --> 15:09.845
<i>How could I not want to
look at his back now!</i>

15:10.096 --> 15:11.555
<i>If I have to trick him,
then so be it…</i>

15:11.973 --> 15:14.892
Oh, it itches… It itches…

15:14.976 --> 15:17.520
If only I could reach it.

15:19.272 --> 15:22.400
I suppose it would be rude
to ask a person I just met

15:22.483 --> 15:24.026
to scratch it for me.

15:26.029 --> 15:27.905
Well, I could help…

15:34.829 --> 15:36.205
JULY 15TH (THURS) 12:28 PM

15:37.373 --> 15:38.415
This is it.

15:38.499 --> 15:41.752
This is where we found
Koichi's bag all by itself.

15:42.003 --> 15:44.588
Koichi's house is less than
two minutes away.

15:45.214 --> 15:48.091
How did this new Stand user storm

15:48.176 --> 15:51.262
Koichi and snatch him
away from a busy school street?

15:51.471 --> 15:53.264
No one saw him.

16:00.021 --> 16:01.230
Josuke…

16:01.272 --> 16:05.772
Our little deal doesn't
assume combat duty by me, correct?

16:05.985 --> 16:07.778
Tracking only, correct?

16:08.529 --> 16:12.741
I won't be fighting any enemies,
correct, Josuke?

16:12.784 --> 16:15.453
Why are you asking me
those questions now?

16:15.787 --> 16:18.289
You were already being tailed.

16:19.415 --> 16:21.166
It's that man.

16:26.297 --> 16:29.383
I smell Koichi's scent on that man.

16:29.425 --> 16:32.469
He has something of Koichi's!

16:34.597 --> 16:37.182
What? That bastard over there?

16:38.476 --> 16:40.478
Wait! Come back here!

16:40.561 --> 16:44.439
You bastard!
What did you do to Koichi?!

16:48.027 --> 16:50.487
M-Mom?

16:52.824 --> 16:54.450
Mom!

16:55.493 --> 16:57.119
It's definitely my mom.

16:57.245 --> 16:58.871
She's out cold, but alive.

16:59.038 --> 17:01.290
<i>I was watching from here,
and still haven't a clue…</i>

17:01.332 --> 17:04.293
<i>When did he change into
Josuke's mom?</i>

17:04.418 --> 17:07.546
<i>I heard Jotaro can stop time
for some two seconds,</i>

17:07.588 --> 17:09.673
<i>but this is
a whole different level!</i>

17:09.757 --> 17:11.467
<i>Even Jotaro wouldn't be able to</i>

17:11.551 --> 17:13.844
<i>swap one person out
with another like that!</i>

17:13.928 --> 17:16.639
If he had just come out and hit me,

17:16.681 --> 17:19.809
I would've been happy
just knocking him out…

17:20.268 --> 17:22.520
But that bastard had to
go after my mom…

17:22.770 --> 17:24.688
Scum like him must be punished!

17:24.772 --> 17:27.399
This scheming scumbag
is gonna feel the pain!

17:27.483 --> 17:29.735
Yuya! Where is the bastard?

17:29.777 --> 17:31.653
Where's that piece of shit hiding?!

17:31.696 --> 17:33.614
If you were touching him
and don't know,

17:33.656 --> 17:35.157
then how would I know?

17:35.241 --> 17:38.535
B-But the guy hasn't left, Josuke…

17:38.619 --> 17:41.747
He's nearby. I can still smell him!

17:43.416 --> 17:46.127
<i>Hmm… Yuya Fungami, huh?</i>

17:46.460 --> 17:49.921
<i>Who knew a simple nose
could work so well.</i>

17:50.173 --> 17:51.424
<i>Well, at least originally,</i>

17:51.465 --> 17:53.675
<i>I initiated my pursuit without
a single care of being caught.</i>

17:54.010 --> 17:56.137
<i>Either way,
releasing Josuke's mother</i>

17:56.179 --> 17:57.722
<i>was all part of the plan…</i>

17:57.805 --> 18:00.641
<i>The perfect plan
to observe Josuke.</i>

18:00.892 --> 18:02.476
<i>Oh observation…</i>

18:03.269 --> 18:06.272
<i>That's what my Stand,
Misterioso, does.</i>

18:06.314 --> 18:09.608
<i>Misterioso meticulously observes</i>

18:09.650 --> 18:12.861
<i>Koichi Hirose and your mother,
as well.</i>

18:13.738 --> 18:17.032
JULY 15TH (THURS) 7:37 AM

18:16.240 --> 18:17.054
God he really pisses me off.

18:19.327 --> 18:21.829
I'll just help myself to his, then!

18:26.000 --> 18:29.086
Josuke! So you are home.

18:29.170 --> 18:30.880
You're here, right?

18:37.762 --> 18:41.140
THESE ARE YOUR PANTIES

18:45.561 --> 18:48.230
No one is immune to fear.

18:49.857 --> 18:53.944
You really shouldn't hide the glow
of fear or the tremors of dread.

18:54.153 --> 18:57.239
The kind of fear that lies
deep in your soul

18:57.365 --> 19:00.076
can never be wiped away…

19:00.117 --> 19:01.409
Not for anyone.

19:01.452 --> 19:04.079
Wh-Who are you?
How did you get in here?

19:06.707 --> 19:09.251
My observations tell me,

19:09.293 --> 19:11.253
when gripped with fear,

19:11.337 --> 19:13.922
you tend to swallow your saliva…

19:14.006 --> 19:16.258
All people exhibit certain
unconscious behaviors

19:16.342 --> 19:18.927
when in a state of panic.

19:19.220 --> 19:22.056
Certain terror-induced quirks…

19:22.139 --> 19:23.890
Did you know you do that?

19:24.642 --> 19:26.268
I said who the hell are you!

19:26.310 --> 19:27.936
I'm not giving you any money!

19:27.979 --> 19:29.188
Get the hell out of here!

19:29.230 --> 19:31.106
Do I look like a burglar?

19:31.232 --> 19:32.983
I don't need your money.

19:33.067 --> 19:34.777
In fact,
I feel like I should pay you.

19:36.195 --> 19:39.573
I'm really quite enjoying myself.

19:39.699 --> 19:43.452
Being the recipient of
so much attention is such a treat.

19:43.661 --> 19:48.040
The attention you're showering me
with out of fear is wonderful.

19:57.717 --> 19:58.843
GULP

19:59.260 --> 20:02.221
Oh? Swallowed again, eh?

20:10.563 --> 20:13.732
See? You just swallowed again!

20:13.899 --> 20:16.735
So that really is
your mark of fear!

20:17.820 --> 20:20.531
Once I discover your mark of fear,

20:21.407 --> 20:25.828
my Misterioso can unleash
its invincible onslaught!

20:41.010 --> 20:47.387
TOMOKO HIGASHIKATA

20:41.135 --> 20:42.803
<i>I've transformed
Tomoko Higashikata,</i>

20:42.845 --> 20:46.056
<i>and Koichi Hirose into paper
with almost no effort a tall!</i>

20:42.887 --> 20:47.387
KOICHI HIROSE

20:46.307 --> 20:48.392
<i>When I gave Koichi a little startle
on his way to school,</i>

20:48.476 --> 20:50.936
<i>I discovered his mark of fear
is a double blink.</i>

20:51.270 --> 20:52.417
<i>It was quite obvious.</i>

20:52.855 --> 20:56.817
Yuya, for the second time,
where is the scent coming from!

20:56.859 --> 21:00.362
<i>I imagined that,
regardless of Josuke's toughness,</i>

21:00.404 --> 21:02.197
<i>plopping his mother before his eyes</i>

21:02.239 --> 21:04.324
<i>would almost certainly
stir pangs of dread…</i>

21:05.659 --> 21:09.287
<i>Sure enough, there was
Josuke's very own mark of fear.</i>

21:09.413 --> 21:13.125
<i>When scared Josuke
bites his lower lip!</i>

21:13.459 --> 21:16.879
<i>The next time Josuke
reveals his mark of fear,</i>

21:15.378 --> 21:19.878
BA-DUMP

21:16.962 --> 21:20.570
<i>Misterioso will eradicate
Josuke from this world!</i>

21:20.758 --> 21:24.052
Yuya, you haven't taken
your eyes off my mom.

21:25.054 --> 21:25.888
Could it be…

21:25.971 --> 21:28.682
Is it this jacket?
Could he be inside this pocket?

21:29.308 --> 21:30.809
I don't care
what kind of Stand it is,

21:30.851 --> 21:32.894
I need to know
is it in this pocket?

21:33.104 --> 21:35.397
<i>Oh? Is he…
Is he gonna bite his lip?!</i>

21:35.481 --> 21:36.648
<i>Come on, bite it!</i>

21:36.690 --> 21:39.025
Yuya, answer me! Is it in here?!

21:39.068 --> 21:41.445
<i>Damn!
Fear hasn't overtaken him yet.</i>

21:42.029 --> 21:46.199
Josuke, I never promised
I'd help you fight.

21:46.242 --> 21:48.285
We agreed tracking only.

21:49.036 --> 21:51.413
It's too freaky
to do anything more.

21:51.455 --> 21:53.832
I agreed to this
cause you healed me,

21:54.041 --> 21:56.418
but no way in hell am I
gonna be an idiot

21:56.460 --> 21:58.086
and walk right into harms way.

21:58.129 --> 22:01.173
I'm sorry,
but this guy freaks me out!

22:04.301 --> 22:05.885
Then I'll have to
find out for myself.

22:07.012 --> 22:10.140
Nothing there.
Both pockets are empty.

22:10.224 --> 22:12.351
Other than this piece of paper…

22:15.479 --> 22:17.606
<i>The scent transferred
to outside the pocket…</i>

22:17.690 --> 22:18.524
<i>Could it be…</i>

22:18.566 --> 22:22.278
<i>Don't! I wouldn't open
that piece of paper!</i>

23:38.896 --> 23:42.024
EPISODE 33
JULY 15TH (THURS), PART 3
